values
  ('capability:admin_normal_technical_mode_split', 'Normal Admin / Technical Admin mode split -- real, live, server-owned toggle', 'Master build brief sections 15-18: the first concrete slice of the Admin IA rebuild. Every real /admin nav item now declares an explicit mode ("normal" | "technical", default normal) alongside its existing release ("v1"|"v2") -- two genuinely orthogonal axes (audience vs maturity), not conflated. New lib/release/admin-view-mode-filter.ts (pure filterNavGroupsByMode, mirrors the existing filterNavGroupsByRelease shape exactly), lib/release/admin-view-mode-pure.ts + admin-view-mode.ts (server-owned httpOnly cookie, mirrors release-mode.ts''s exact pattern), app/api/admin/view-mode/route.ts (owner-admin-only POST/GET, mirrors release-mode/route.ts exactly, audit-logged), and components/shell/AdminViewModeToggle.tsx (a second switch in the admin top bar, alongside the existing Stable/Beta toggle). admin-nav-data.ts fully recategorized: Normal = Home, Admin Copilot, Clients, Social Autopilot (Growth), Leads/CRM + Go Free Codes (Sales), Finance, Approvals + Human Handoffs + Audit Delivery (Tasks), Team (Settings). Technical = My Operating Brain + Capability Registry (Brain), All Missions + Hermes Mission Control (Missions), Integrations (Connections), Operations Queue (Jobs & Queues -- closest real surface; no dedicated Jobs/Queues/Workers page exists yet), System Health + Audit Log (System). No functionality removed -- every one of the 19 real pre-existing nav items still resolves in exactly one mode (asserted by a real test). No empty placeholder pages invented for brief-named slots with no real page (Agents/Skills/Workers/APIs/Deployments/Recovery) -- honestly absent, not faked. Also found and removed one genuinely dead file while starting this work: app/admin/platform/layout.tsx (see capability:admin_ia_cleanup_dead_platform_layout) -- an orphaned pre-"Phase 1 migration" leftover with zero real page.tsx anywhere in its own subtree.', 'ecosystem', null, null, 'lib/release/admin-view-mode-filter.ts, admin-view-mode-pure.ts, admin-view-mode.ts, app/api/admin/view-mode/route.ts, components/shell/AdminViewModeToggle.tsx, components/shell/navigation/admin-nav-data.ts, admin-navigation.tsx, nav-types.ts, app/admin/(shell)/AppShell.tsx, app/admin/(shell)/layout.tsx', 'Engineering', null, null, 'read', 'platform_only', 'free', 'low_mutation', 'New admin-view-mode-architecture.test.ts (real assertions: pure helper fail-closed defaults, mutual exclusivity of Normal/Technical across every real nav item, zero functionality lost, cookie/gate/toggle contract). Fixed a real, correct assertion in the pre-existing (but never-wired-into-any-npm-script until this pass -- also fixed) v1-stable-beta-architecture.test.ts, which asserted a literal "Beta" group label that the redesign intentionally replaced with real subject-based grouping (Brain, Missions). Both now wired into a new test:admin-view-mode script. Full test:unified-shell-crm and test:hermes-mission-control suites still pass. Full-repo tsc --noEmit clean, lint clean, real NODE_ENV=production next build exit 0.', 'REAL_EXPOSED', 'Backend/data-model complete and live: the toggle, cookie, API route, and full nav recategorization are real and functional today. Still open, tracked separately: the Premium UI visual pass (shadcn/Radix/Lucide/Tremor, sections 19-20), the rebuilt Admin Home content (section 17), and live UI verification by actually opening the deployed page (section 28) -- this entry will be updated once that verification runs.', null, now(), 'claude_session_2026-09-02')
